<title>USA: Intermedia Communications completes merger.</title>
<headline>Intermedia Communications completes merger.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPA, Fla. 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intermedia Communications said Monday, its wholly owned subsidiary, Daylight Acquisition Corp, completed the purchase of DIGEX Inc, a nationwide business internet access provider, for $150 million in cash.  Intermedia said it also converted the equivalent of $20 million worth of outstanding DIGEX options into Intermedia options.</p>
<p>Intermedia purchased 98.8 percent of DIGEX shares in its tender offer which ended July 9, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>DIGEX shareholders were originally offered $13 dollars for each of their shares, Intermedia told Reuters.</p>
